From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:50:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Input: chipone-icnl9922c - mask IRQ unlazily and clear
 pending IRQ on resume

The ICNL9922C TDDI touchscreen uses an edge-falling EINT interrupt.
During panel sleep/reset and volatile SRAM firmware upload on resume,
the INT line toggles and latches a pending interrupt in the controller.
Without IRQ_DISABLE_UNLAZY and clearing IRQCHIP_STATE_PENDING prior to
enable_irq(), the stale latched interrupt fires immediately after resume
and reads all-0x7f SPI idle bytes ("touch read failed: -5").

Set IRQ_DISABLE_UNLAZY when requesting the IRQ and clear any pending
hardware interrupt state immediately before re-enabling the IRQ at the
end of icnl9922c_fw_work().

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
index d960b66bd..5c2d9a81e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/input/mt.h>
 #include <linux/input/touchscreen.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/irq.h>
 #include <linux/math.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
@@ -520,6 +521,7 @@ static int icnl9922c_ensure_input(struct icnl9922c_ts *ts, u16 fwid, u16 fwver,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	irq_set_status_flags(ts->spi->irq, IRQ_DISABLE_UNLAZY);
 	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, ts->spi->irq, NULL,
 					icnl9922c_irq_handler,
 					IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_NO_AUTOEN,
@@ -713,6 +715,7 @@ static void icnl9922c_fw_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 	mutex_lock(&ts->lock);
 	if (ts->running && !ts->irq_enabled) {
+		irq_set_irqchip_state(ts->spi->irq, IRQCHIP_STATE_PENDING, false);
 		enable_irq(ts->spi->irq);
 		ts->irq_enabled = true;
 	}
